From a5d4d53e11b4f07d5f98dfb3438c0103af74f7ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 18:09:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 253/350] Start page: four ways to start, the search, and first
 steps for people new to CAD
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

In the integrated environment the start page asks "What do you want to
make?": a new part, a new assembly, a drawing (of the open part, or of a
file opened first) or a file to open (STEP, DXF, DWG, Jw_cad, STL …), each
one click from its first screen. Below them, the tool search. At the right,
"New to CAD? (5 minutes)": four short walks (a plate with holes, changing
a size afterwards, putting STEP parts together, a JIS drawing), each with
its sample made on the spot and its steps at the right of the window,
ticked off as the user does them (FirstSteps.py). The first-start settings
and "do not show again" are no longer at the bottom of the page.

The band of a step finds the OK and Cancel of the panel on screen (boxes
of closed panels may still exist), so the panel's own pair is always hidden.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
